@Candyss.Love, I learned the basics of traveling long-term, saved money for more than a year, and bought a one-way ticket, At first i lived off of my savings for a few months - long term travel can be very inexpensive, But i wanted to keep traveling so i started freelancing. It was slow at first but kept me afloat. , You do not need to work as a freelancer to travel -
I lived off my savings for months, But if you want to be a digital nomad there are infinite ways to make money as a freelancer / remote employee, Then you can travel forever :)

How to Travel 
WITHOUT PAYING
for a stay, Work/ Travel for free:)

